[ERR] 2026-01-24 11:48:37 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': 'cat > /tmp/stdmae_analysis.md << \'EOF\'\n# STD-MAE Repository Analysis Report\n\n## Repository Information\n- **Model**: STD-MAE (Spatial-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Autoencoder for Traffic Forecasting)\n- **Repository URL**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/STD-MAE\n- **Cloned to**: /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE\n- **Publication**: IJCAI-24 (Thirty-Third International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence)\n- **ArXiv**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00516\n- **Paper Link**: https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/0442.pdf\n\n## Framework & Dependencies\n\n### Python & Core Framework\n- **Python Version**: 3.9\n- **PyTorch Version**: 1.13.1\n- **Framework**: PyTorch-based (Neural Network Architecture)\n\n### Key Dependencies (from requirements.txt)\n```\neasy_torch==1.2.12          # Framework wrapper\neasydict==1.10              # Configuration management\nnumpy==1.21.5               # Numerical computing\npositional_encodings==6.0.1 # Positional encoding layers\nscikit_learn==1.0.2         # Machine learning utilities\nscipy==1.7.3                # Scientific computing\nsetproctitle==1.3.2         # Process naming\nsympy==1.10.1               # Symbolic mathematics\ntimm==0.6.11                # Timm vision models (for truncated normal init)\ntorch==1.13.1               # Core PyTorch\ntorch_summary==1.4.5        # Model summary visualization\ntvm==1.0.0                  # TensorFlow VM\n```\n\n### Framework Build Information\n- **Base Framework**: BasicTS (https://github.com/zezhishao/BasicTS)\n- **Execution Framework**: EasyTorch (https://github.com/cnstark/easytorch)\n\n## Model Architecture\n\n### Overview\nSTD-MAE implements a **Spatial-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Autoencoder** architecture that combines:\n1. **Temporal MAE (T-MAE)**: Masks and reconstructs temporal patterns\n2. **Spatial MAE (S-MAE)**: Masks and reconstructs spatial patterns\n3. **Backend Predictor**: Graph WaveNet for final forecasting\n\n### Architecture Components\n\n#### 1. Main Model Class\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE/stdmae/stdmae_arch/stdmae.py`\n\n```python\nclass STDMAE(nn.Module):\n    """Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting"""\n    \n    def __init__(self, dataset_name, pre_trained_tmae_path, pre_trained_smae_path, \n                 mask_args, backend_args):\n        # Components:\n        self.tmae = Mask(**mask_args)              # Temporal MAE module\n        self.smae = Mask(**mask_args)              # Spatial MAE module\n        self.backend = GraphWaveNet(**backend_args) # Prediction backend\n```\n\n**Key Method**:\n- `forward()`: Processes history data through decoupled MAE modules, concatenates features, and uses GraphWaveNet for final prediction\n\n**Input/Output Shapes**:\n- **Input**: \n  - `history_data`: [B, L, N, 3] (batch, sequence_length, num_nodes, features)\n  - `long_history_data`: [B, L*P, N, 3] (long-term history for MAE pre-training)\n- **Output**: [B, L, N, 1] (traffic prediction)\n\n#### 2. Core Masked Autoencoder (Mask Module)\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE/stdmae/stdmae_arch/mask/mask.py`\n\n```python\nclass Mask(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, patch_size, in_channel, embed_dim, num_heads, mlp_ratio, \n                 dropout, mask_ratio, encoder_depth, decoder_depth, spatial=False, \n                 mode="pre-train"):\n```\n\n**Hyperparameter Configuration** (from STDMAE_PEMS03.py):\n```python\nmask_args = {\n    "patch_size": 12,            # Temporal/Spatial patch size\n    "in_channel": 1,             # Input channels (traffic flow)\n    "embed_dim": 96,             # Embedding dimension\n    "num_heads": 4,              # Attention heads\n    "mlp_ratio": 4,              # MLP ratio in transformer\n    "dropout": 0.1,              # Dropout rate\n    "mask_ratio": 0.25,          # Masking ratio (25% for forecasting, 75% for pre-training)\n    "encoder_depth": 4,          # Transformer encoder layers\n    "decoder_depth": 1,          # Transformer decoder layers\n    "mode": "forecasting"        # or "pre-train"\n}\n```\n\n**Architecture Flow**:\n\n1. **Patch Embedding** (`PatchEmbedding`):\n   - Uses Conv2d with kernel (patch_size, 1) to create patches\n   - Input: [B, N, 1, L*P] → Output: [B, N, embed_dim, P]\n   - Temporal patches: Each patch is 12 timesteps\n   - Spatial patches: Each patch is 12 nodes\n\n2. **Masking Strategy**:\n   - **Temporal Masking** (T-MAE): Masks timesteps along temporal dimension\n     - Input shape: [B, N, P, d] (patches)\n     - MaskGenerator selects unmasked tokens from temporal patches\n     - Mask ratio determines percentage masked\n   \n   - **Spatial Masking** (S-MAE): Masks nodes along spatial dimension\n     - Input shape: [B, N, P, d] transposed to [B, P, N, d]\n     - MaskGenerator selects unmasked nodes\n     - Only spatial information masked, temporal intact\n\n3. **Positional Encoding** (`PositionalEncoding`):\n   - Uses PositionalEncoding2D from positional_encodings library\n   - Adds absolute positional information to patches\n   - Output includes both position-augmented data and position matrix\n\n4. **Encoder** (`TransformerLayers`):\n   - Multi-head attention transformer encoder\n   - Processes unmasked tokens only during pre-training\n   - Outputs hidden states for masked token reconstruction\n   - Pre-training mode: sparse input (only unmasked tokens)\n   - Forecasting mode: full input (all tokens)\n\n5. **Mask Token**:\n   - Learnable parameter for masked positions\n   - Shape: (1, 1, 1, embed_dim)\n   - Initialized with truncated normal distribution\n\n6. **Decoder** (`TransformerLayers`):\n   - Lower depth (1 layer) than encoder\n   - Reconstructs full sequence (unmasked + masked tokens)\n   - Outputs embeddings for reconstruction\n\n7. **Output Layer**:\n   - Linear projection: embed_dim → patch_size\n   - Reconstructs patch values\n\n**Forward Process**:\n\n**Pre-training Mode** (Temporal MAE or Spatial MAE):\n```\nInput: long_history_data [B, N, 1, L*P]\n  ↓\nPatch Embedding: → [B, N, embed_dim, P]\n  ↓\nPositional Encoding (add position info)\n  ↓\nMasking (mask_ratio=0.75 for pre-training)\n  ↓\nEncoder (only unmasked tokens)\n  ↓\nDecoder (combines unmasked + mask tokens)\n  ↓\nOutput Layer (reconstruct patch values)\n  ↓\nLoss: MAE between reconstructed and ground-truth masked patches\n```\n\n**Forecasting Mode**:\n```\nInput: long_history_data [B, N, 1, L*P]\n  ↓\nPatch Embedding & Positional Encoding\n  ↓\nEncoder (processes full sequence, no masking)\n  ↓\nOutput: Hidden states [B, N, P, embed_dim]\n  ↓\n(Used as features for downstream predictor)\n```\n\n#### 3. Mask Generator\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE/stdmae/stdmae_arch/mask/maskgenerator.py`\n\n```python\nclass MaskGenerator(nn.Module):\n    def uniform_rand(self):\n        # Randomly shuffles tokens and splits at mask_ratio\n        # Returns: (unmasked_tokens_indices, masked_tokens_indices)\n```\n\n- **Strategy**: Uniform random masking\n- **Implementation**: Shuffles token indices and splits by mask_ratio\n- **Sorting**: Sorts indices for deterministic processing\n\n#### 4. Temporal vs Spatial Masking\n\n**Key Difference in Implementation**:\n\nIn `mask.py` `encoding()` method:\n```python\nif self.spatial:\n    # Spatial masking: mask along node dimension\n    patches = patches.transpose(-1, -2)  # [B, N, P, d] → [B, P, N, d]\n    MaskGenerator(patches.shape[1], mask_ratio)  # Mask over N nodes\n    \nif not self.spatial:\n    # Temporal masking: mask along time dimension\n    MaskGenerator(patches.shape[2], mask_ratio)  # Mask over P timestamps\n```\n\n- **T-MAE** (`spatial=False`):Masks different time patches\n- **S-MAE** (`spatial=True`): Masks different spatial nodes\n- Both use identical Mask architecture with different masking dimensions\n\n#### 5. Backend Predictor: Graph WaveNet\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE/stdmae/stdmae_arch/graphwavenet/model.py`\n\n**Configuration** (from STDMAE_PEMS03.py):\n```python\nbackend_args = {\n    "num_nodes": 358,                    # PEMS03 has 358 nodes\n    "supports": [adj_mx tensors],        # Pre-computed adjacency matrices\n    "dropout": 0.3,\n    "gcn_bool": True,                    # Use graph convolution\n    "addaptadj": True,                   # Learnable adjacency matrix\n    "aptinit": None,\n    "in_dim": 2,                         # Input: T-MAE + S-MAE features\n    "out_dim": 12,                       # Output: 12 timesteps\n    "residual_channels": 32,\n    "dilation_channels": 32,\n    "skip_channels": 256,\n    "end_channels": 512,\n    "kernel_size": 2,\n    "blocks": 4,\n    "layers": 2\n}\n```\n\n**Architecture Features**:\n- Graph convolution network layers for spatial modeling\n- Dilated causal convolutions for temporal modeling\n- Adaptive adjacency matrix learning\n- Multi-layer residual structure\n\n## Training Pipeline\n\n### Three-Stage Training\n\n#### Stage 1: Temporal MAE Pre-training (T-MAE)\n**Config**: `stdmae/TMAE_PEMS03.py`\n- **Task**: Reconstruct masked temporal patches\n- **Mask Ratio**: 0.25 (pre-training) or 0.75 (depends on config)\n- **Epochs**: 200\n- **Learning Rate**: 0.001\n- **Output**: `mask_save/TMAE_PEMS03_864.pt`\n\n#### Stage 2: Spatial MAE Pre-training (S-MAE)\n**Config**: `stdmae/SMAE_PEMS03.py`\n- **Task**: Reconstruct masked spatial patches\n- **Mask Ratio**: 0.25 (forecast) or 0.75 (pre-training)\n- **Similar setup to T-MAE**\n- **Output**: `mask_save/SMAE_PEMS03_864.pt`\n\n#### Stage 3: Downstream Forecasting (STD-MAE)\n**Config**: `stdmae/STDMAE_PEMS03.py`\n- **Task**: Traffic forecasting with frozen MAE encoders\n- **Input**: Concatenated [T-MAE features + S-MAE features]\n- **Backend**: GraphWaveNet\n- **Pre-trained checkpoints**: Loaded from mask_save/ directory\n- **Epochs**: 300\n- **Learning Rate**: 0.002\n- **Curriculum Learning**: 6 epochs warmup + gradual length increase\n\n### Training Configuration\n**File**: `stdmae/STDMAE_PEMS03.py`\n\n```python\nCFG.TRAIN = {\n    "LOSS": masked_mae,\n    "OPTIM": {\n        "TYPE": "Adam",\n        "lr": 0.002,\n        "weight_decay": 1.0e-5,\n        "eps": 1.0e-8\n    },\n    "LR_SCHEDULER": {\n        "TYPE": "MultiStepLR",\n        "milestones": [1, 18, 36, 54, 72],\n        "gamma": 0.5\n    },\n    "CLIP_GRAD": {"max_norm": 3.0},\n    "NUM_EPOCHS": 300\n}\n```\n\n### Data Configuration\n- **Input Length** (history): 12 timesteps\n- **Output Length** (forecast): 12 timesteps\n- **Long-term History**: 288*3 = 864 timesteps (3 days for pre-training)\n- **Batch Size**: 8\n- **Datasets Supported**: PEMS03, PEMS04, PEMS07, PEMS08, PEMS-BAY, METR-LA, PEMSD7M, PEMSD7L, EXPY-TKY\n\n## Data Format & Requirements\n\n### Input Data Format\n**File**: `stdmae/stdmae_data/forecasting_dataset.py`\n\n```python\nclass ForecastingDataset:\n    # Returns: (future_data, history_data, long_history_data)\n    # Shapes:\n    # - future_data: [L, N, C] (12, num_nodes, features)\n    # - history_data: [L, N, C] (12, num_nodes, features)\n    # - long_history_data: [seq_len, N, C] (864, num_nodes, features)\n```\n\n**Data Structure**:\n- Loads from pickle files: `data.pkl` (processed normalized data)\n- Index file: `index.pkl` (train/val/test split indices)\n- Adjacency matrix: `adj_mx.pkl` (graph structure)\n\n**Preprocessing**:\n- Data is normalized during preprocessing\n- Scripts for data preparation in `scripts/data_preparation/all.sh`\n\n### Expected Datasets\nAll PEMS (Performance Evaluation of Advanced Traffic Monitoring Systems) datasets:\n- **PEMS03**: 358 nodes\n- **PEMS04**: 307 nodes\n- **PEMS07**: 883 nodes\n- **PEMS08**: 170 nodes\n- **PEMS-BAY**: 325 nodes\n- **METR-LA**: 207 nodes\n- **PEMSD7M**: larger PEMS07 variant\n- **PEMSD7L**: largest PEMS07 variant\n- **EXPY-TKY**: Tokyo expressway data\n\n## File Structure\n\n### Core Model Files\n```\n/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/STD-MAE/\n├── stdmae/\n│   ├── run.py                          # Entry point script\n│   ├── stdmae_arch/\n│   │   ├── stdmae.py                   # STDMAE main model (combines T-MAE + S-MAE + backend)\n│   │   ├── mask/\n│   │   │   ├── mask.py                 # Core Mask autoencoder module\n│   │   │   ├── maskgenerator.py        # Mask generation strategy\n│   │   │   ├── patch.py                # Patch embedding (patchification)\n│   │   │   ├── positional_encoding.py  # Positional encoding layers\n│   │   │   └── transformer_layers.py   # Transformer encoder/decoder\n│   │   └── graphwavenet/\n│   │       └── model.py                # GraphWaveNet backend predictor\n│   ├── stdmae_data/\n│   │   ├── forecasting_dataset.py      # Forecasting stage dataset\n│   │   └── pretraining_dataset.py      # Pre-training stage dataset\n│   ├── stdmae_runner/\n│   │   ├── mask_runner.py              # Runner for pre-training\n│   │   └── stdmae_runner.py            # Runner for downstream forecasting\n│   ├── TMAE_PEMS*.py                   # Temporal MAE configs (8 datasets)\n│   ├── SMAE_PEMS*.py                   # Spatial MAE configs (8 datasets)\n│   └── STDMAE_PEMS*.py                 # Downstream forecasting configs (8 datasets)\n└── basicts/                            # BasicTS framework implementation\n```\n\n### Configuration Files\n- **Pre-training Config**: `TMAE_PEMS03.py` (temporal masking)\n- **Pre-training Config**: `SMAE_PEMS03.py` (spatial masking)\n- **Forecasting Config**: `STDMAE_PEMS03.py` (downstream task)\n\n### Data Files\n```\ndatasets/\n├── PEMS03/\n│   ├── data.pkl           # Processed and normalized traffic data\n│   ├── index.pkl          # Train/val/test split indices\n│   ├── adj_mx.pkl         # Adjacency matrix (multiple representations)\n│   └── raw_data/\n```\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### Attention Mechanisms\n- **Multi-Head Attention**: 4 heads in transformer 