Backend for spatial-temporal modeling\n  - Integrates T-MAE and S-MAE features via FC layers\n  - Adaptive adjacency matrix support\n  - WaveNet-style dilated convolutions\n\n## Architecture Flow\n\n```\nInput: [B, T, N, C] (Batch, Time, Nodes, Channels)\n    |\n    v\n[Reshape to MAE format] -> [B, N, C, T]\n    |\n    |---> T-MAE Encoder (temporal) -> [B, N, P, 96]\n    |\n    |---> S-MAE Encoder (spatial)  -> [B, N, P, 96]\n    |\n    v\nConcatenate -> [B, N, P, 192]\n    |\n    v\nExtract last patch -> [B, N, 192]\n    |\n    v\nGraphWaveNet Backend (with short-term history)\n    |\n    v\nOutput: [B, T_out, N, 1]\n```\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n### 1. Data Format Transformation\n- **Original**: Separate `history_data` and `long_history_data` parameters\n- **LibCity**: Single batch dict with keys `\'X\'` and `\'y\'`\n- **Solution**: Extract features from batch dict and reshape as needed\n\n### 2. Model Initialization\n- **Original**: Separate config dicts for `mask_args` and `backend_args`\n- **LibCity**: Unified config object\n- **Solution**: Extract all parameters from single config object with defaults\n\n### 3. Pre-trained Checkpoints\n- **Original**: Requires pre-trained T-MAE and S-MAE checkpoints\n- **LibCity**: May not have checkpoints available\n- **Solution**:\n  - Accept optional checkpoint paths via config\n  - Gracefully handle missing checkpoints with warning\n  - Continue with random initialization if checkpoints unavailable\n\n### 4. Loss Function\n- **Original**: Custom masked loss in runner\n- **LibCity**: `calculate_loss()` method in model\n- **Solution**: Use `loss.masked_mae_torch()` from LibCity\'s loss module\n\n### 5. Adjacency Matrix\n- **Original**: Passed as parameter to GraphWaveNet\n- **LibCity**: Extracted from `data_feature[\'adj_mx\']`\n- **Solution**: Extract from data_feature and convert to tensor list\n\n### 6. Device Handling\n- **Original**: Explicit device assignment\n- **LibCity**: Device from config\n- **Solution**: Use `config.get(\'device\')` and move tensors appropriately\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Required Parameters\n```json\n{\n  "num_nodes": 207,\n  "feature_dim": 1,\n  "output_dim": 1,\n  "input_window": 12,\n  "output_window": 12,\n  "device": "cuda:0"\n}\n```\n\n### Model-Specific Parameters (with defaults)\n```json\n{\n  "patch_size": 12,\n  "embed_dim": 96,\n  "num_heads": 4,\n  "mlp_ratio": 4,\n  "dropout": 0.1,\n  "mask_ratio": 0.25,\n  "encoder_depth": 4,\n  "decoder_depth": 1,\n  "blocks": 4,\n  "layers": 2,\n  "gcn_bool": true,\n  "addaptadj": true,\n  "kernel_size": 2,\n  "residual_channels": 32,\n  "dilation_channels": 32,\n  "skip_channels": 256,\n  "end_channels": 512\n}\n```\n\n### Optional Parameters\n```json\n{\n  "pre_trained_tmae_path": "/path/to/tmae_checkpoint.pth",\n  "pre_trained_smae_path": "/path/to/smae_checkpoint.pth"\n}\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### External Libraries Required\n1. **timm**: For `trunc_normal_` initialization\n   ```bash\n   pip install timm\n   ```\n\n2. **positional-encodings**: For 2D positional encoding\n   ```bash\n   pip install positional-encodings[pytorch]\n   ```\n\n### LibCity Built-in\n- `torch`, `torch.nn`, `torch.nn.functional`\n- `libcity.model.abstract_traffic_state_model.AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n- `libcity.model.loss`\n\n## Pre-trained Checkpoint Files\n\n### Location (Original Repo)\n- T-MAE checkpoints: `checkpoints/STDMAE_*/[DATASET]/T-MAE_[DATASET].pth`\n- S-MAE checkpoints: `checkpoints/STDMAE_*/[DATASET]/S-MAE_[DATASET].pth`\n\n### Expected Format\n```python\n{\n    \'model_state_dict\': {...},  # Model parameters\n    # Optional: \'optimizer_state_dict\', \'epoch\', etc.\n}\n```\n\n### Datasets with Pre-trained Models\n- PEMS03, PEMS04, PEMS07, PEMS08\n- PEMSD7M, PEMSD7L\n- METR-LA, PEMS-BAY\n- EXPY-TKY\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **Long History Requirement**:\n   - Original model uses both short-term (12 steps) and long-term history (for pre-training)\n   - Current adaptation uses short-term history for GraphWaveNet\n   - MAE encoders process the same short-term history\n\n2. **Pre-training Not Implemented**:\n   - Only forecasting mode is implemented\n   - Pre-training mode (for creating MAE checkpoints) requires separate implementation\n   - Users must provide pre-trained checkpoints or use random initialization\n\n3. **Patch Size Fixed**:\n   - Default patch size is 12 timesteps\n   - Input window should be divisible by patch_size\n   - Non-divisible inputs may cause dimension mismatch errors\n\n4. **Memory Usage**:\n   - Dual transformer encoders (T-MAE + S-MAE) consume significant memory\n   - GraphWaveNet backend adds additional overhead\n   - Consider reducing `embed_dim`, `encoder_depth`, or batch size for large graphs\n\n## Testing Recommendations\n\n1. **Import Test**:\n   ```python\n   from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STDMAE import STDMAE\n   ```\n\n2. **Initialization Test**:\n   ```python\n   config = {...}  # Configuration dict\n   data_feature = {...}  # Data features\n   model = STDMAE(config, data_feature)\n   ```\n\n3. **Forward Pass Test**:\n   ```python\n   batch = {\n       \'X\': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 1),\n       \'y\': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 1)\n   }\n   output = model(batch)\n   loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n   ```\n\n4. **Checkpoint Loading Test**:\n   ```python\n   # Test with valid checkpoint paths\n   config[\'pre_trained_tmae_path\'] = \'/path/to/checkpoint\'\n   model = STDMAE(config, data_feature)\n   ```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Configuration File**: Create LibCity config JSON file (e.g., `STDMAE.json`)\n2. **Integration Test**: Test with actual LibCity executor and data pipeline\n3. **Performance Tuning**: Adjust hyperparameters for specific datasets\n4. **Checkpoint Setup**: Prepare or train pre-trained MAE checkpoints\n5. **Documentation**: Add model to LibCity\'s model documentation\n\n## Registration Status\n\nThe model is already registered in:\n- `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\nThe import line exists:\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STDMAE import STDMAE\n```\n\nAnd it\'s in the `__all__` list:\n```python\n__all__ = [..., "STDMAE", ...]\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nSuccessfully adapted STD-MAE to LibCity with:\n- ✅ Full LibCity API compliance (AbstractTrafficStateModel)\n- ✅ Proper batch dict handling\n- ✅ Graceful checkpoint loading with fallback\n- ✅ All supporting components integrated\n- ✅ Model registered in __init__.py\n- ✅ Compatible loss function (masked MAE)\n- ✅ Device handling\n- ✅ Comprehensive documentation\n\nThe model is ready for configuration and testing within the LibCity framework.\n'}
