nds\n\n### Training\n```python\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.0005)\nfor epoch in range(max_epoch):\n    for batch in train_loader:\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n        loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n```\n\n### Inference\n```python\nmodel.eval()\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    predictions = model.predict(batch)\n```\n\n### GPU Usage\n```python\nconfig[\'device\'] = torch.device(\'cuda:0\')\nmodel = STDMAE(config, data_feature)\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: Shape Mismatch\n```\nSolution: Ensure input_window % patch_size == 0\nExample: input_window=12, patch_size=12 (OK)\n         input_window=24, patch_size=12 (OK)\n         input_window=11, patch_size=12 (WRONG)\n```\n\n### Issue: Out of Memory\n```\nSolutions:\n1. Reduce batch_size: 32 → 16 → 8\n2. Reduce embed_dim: 96 → 64 → 32\n3. Reduce encoder_depth: 4 → 2\n4. Use checkpoint gradient: model.gradient_checkpointing_enable()\n```\n\n### Issue: Checkpoint Not Loading\n```\n- Model will use random initialization\n- Check logs for warning message\n- Verify checkpoint path and format\n```\n\n## Files Map\n\n| Purpose | Location |\n|---------|----------|\n| Model Code | `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STDMAE.py` |\n| Components | `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STDMAE_Components.py` |\n| Config | `libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STDMAE.json` |\n| Tests | `test_stdmae_import.py` |\n| Docs | `documentation/STDMAE_*.md` |\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n```bash\n# For GPU\nexport CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0\n\n# For reproducibility\nexport PYTHONHASHSEED=0\n```\n\n## Dataset Requirements\n\n- Adjacency matrix (adj_mx)\n- Data scaler\n- Number of nodes\n- Feature dimensions\n\n## Performance Tips\n\n### For Better Results\n1. Use pre-trained checkpoints\n2. Increase embed_dim (96→128)\n3. Increase encoder_depth (4→6)\n4. Use higher learning_rate (0.001 vs 0.0005)\n\n### For Faster Training\n1. Reduce embed_dim (96→64)\n2. Reduce encoder_depth (4→2)\n3. Use larger batch_size if memory allows\n4. Enable gradient checkpointing\n\n## Parameter Ranges\n\n| Parameter | Min | Default | Max | Notes |\n|-----------|-----|---------|-----|-------|\n| embed_dim | 32 | 96 | 256 | Must be divisible by num_heads |\n| num_heads | 1 | 4 | 8 | embed_dim must be divisible by this |\n| encoder_depth | 1 | 4 | 12 | Deeper = more capacity |\n| blocks | 1 | 4 | 8 | Deeper = more capacity |\n| layers | 1 | 2 | 4 | Deeper = more capacity |\n| dropout | 0.0 | 0.1 | 0.5 | Higher = more regularization |\n| learning_rate | 1e-5 | 5e-4 | 1e-2 | Dataset dependent |\n\n## Batch Size Guide\n\n| Scenario | Recommended |\n|----------|------------|\n| Small GPU (2GB) | 8-16 |\n| Medium GPU (8GB) | 32-64 |\n| Large GPU (24GB) | 64-128 |\n| Multiple GPUs | 128+ |\n\n## Dataset-Specific Configs\n\n### METR-LA\n```json\n{"num_nodes": 207, "learning_rate": 0.0005, "batch_size": 32}\n```\n\n### PEMS-BAY\n```json\n{"num_nodes": 325, "learning_rate": 0.0005, "batch_size": 32}\n```\n\n### PEMS04\n```json\n{"num_nodes": 307, "learning_rate": 0.0005, "batch_size": 32}\n```\n\n### PEMS08\n```json\n{"num_nodes": 170, "learning_rate": 0.0005, "batch_size": 32}\n```\n\n## Monitoring\n\n### Important Metrics\n```python\n# Loss\nloss_train, loss_val = ...\n\n# MAE, RMSE, MAPE\nmetrics = calculate_metrics(predictions, targets)\n\n# Learning rate\ncurrent_lr = optimizer.param_groups[0][\'lr\']\n```\n\n### Logging\n```python\nlogger.info(f"Epoch {epoch}: loss={loss.item():.4f}")\nlogger.info(f"Model has {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())} parameters")\n```\n\n## Device Compatibility\n\n- ✅ CPU (slow but works)\n- ✅ Single GPU (recommended)\n- ⚠️ Multiple GPUs (requires DataParallel wrapper)\n- ✅ Mixed precision (use torch.autocast)\n\n## Memory Estimation\n\nFor METR-LA (207 nodes) with batch_size=32:\n- Model weights: ~20 MB\n- Forward pass: ~2-3 GB\n- Backward pass: ~4-5 GB\n- **Total needed**: ~8 GB\n\n## Common Errors & Fixes\n\n| Error | Fix |\n|-------|-----|\n| `ImportError: No module named \'timm\'` | `pip install timm` |\n| `ImportError: positional_encodings` | `pip install positional-encodings[pytorch]` |\n| `RuntimeError: CUDA out of memory` | Reduce batch_size, embed_dim, or depth |\n| `Shape mismatch` | Ensure input_window % patch_size == 0 |\n| `IndexError in masking` | Check patch_size value |\n\n## Quick Start Checklist\n\n- [ ] Install timm and positional-encodings\n- [ ] Run test_stdmae_import.py\n- [ ] Prepare dataset with adjacency matrix\n- [ ] Configure model parameters\n- [ ] Set device (GPU/CPU)\n- [ ] Prepare data loaders\n- [ ] Initialize optimizer\n- [ ] Run training loop\n- [ ] Evaluate on test set\n\n## Support Resources\n\n1. **Adaptation Report**: `documentation/STDMAE_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md`\n2. **Config Guide**: `documentation/STDMAE_CONFIG_PARAMS.md`\n3. **File Summary**: `documentation/STDMAE_FILES_SUMMARY.md`\n4. **Complete Summary**: `documentation/STDMAE_COMPLETE_SUMMARY.md`\n5. **Test Script**: `test_stdmae_import.py`\n\n---\n**Version**: 1.0 | **Updated**: 2026-01-24\n'}
